  "name": "mkcx",
  "description": "mkcx is a context curation engine designed to synthesize high-fidelity prompts for one-shot LLM software engineering workflows. It integrates a CLI for multi-source ingestion from Local, Crates.io, GitHub, and Opam sources with a background daemon, mkcxd, that manages vector embeddings and semantic context compression. The system employs advanced summarization strategies and trait implementation ablations to optimize token usage while preserving critical architectural intent for large-scale model reasoning.",
